tional  organization  llama or nu the enu was already  anti-communist but to further motivate  them army officers circulated the news  that pkl activists held hit lists of  islamic leaders from the perspective of  the ansar it was a case of kill or be  killed the answer was not alone the army  mobilized now members of the catholic  and nationalist parties most of these  militias operated in rural areas an  armed band would target a village  suspected of supporting the pki they  would surround it seize party members  and sympathizers and detain them in  temporary detention centers where  prisoners were tortured and interrogated  what happened next is best described by  a chilling declassified cable sent by  edwardi masters political affairs  councillor at the u.s embassy in jakarta  on the 30th of november 965 he wrote  repression of the phi continued with the  main problem that's of what to feed and  where to house the prisoners many  provinces appear to be successfully  meeting the problem by executing their  pki prisoners or killing them before  they are captured prisoners were marched  into the forests for the final act they  were shot stabbed beaten to death and  their bodies dumped into mass graves in  many cases bodies were thrown into  rivers or left to rot in the streets to  further terrorize local populations  militias took to mutilating corpses and  leaving their heads and genitals in full  view  the purges continued into 1966 while no  documents have proven that zahato  directly ordered the killings he was at  the top of the chain of command and  directed the actions of the paratroopers  and the training of the militias  professor russa guesses that zahato must  have at least approved of the massacres  according to professor brad simpson  university of connecticut the  extermination of the pki propelled his  career even further socano far from  doing anything concrete to stop the  bloodshed confirmed sahato's status as  commander-in-chief and on the 11th 